{
  "_comment": [
    "Inputs for the test pack, assembled at test time. No .rpgpack binary is committed:",
    "a pack is a SQLite file, opaque in review and useless in a diff, and storing the",
    "inputs as text means a schema change updates the fixture automatically instead of",
    "waiting for someone to remember to rebuild a binary.",
    "",
    "Chunks are located by ANCHORS rather than by byte offsets. The spec says 'spans',",
    "and the pack the builder emits carries real UTF-8 byte spans -- but hand-written",
    "offsets silently rot the moment a word changes in the source, which defeats the",
    "reason for storing the fixture as text at all. An anchor that no longer matches, or",
    "that matches twice, fails the build loudly instead.",
    "",
    "Emberlight is an original miniature RPG written for this repository, not a real",
    "published SRD. It is here because the corpus needs rules, lore, tables, statblocks,",
    "and a second book to exercise every route, and because it can be licensed freely",
    "without anyone's permission. Swapping in a real open-licensed SRD is a change to",
    "this directory and nothing else."
  ],
